"Sums of Polynomials and Clique Roots (https://arxiv.org/abs/2112.09744)\nciteturn1academia12 [wordlim: 200] Published: 4.9 years ago; Title: Sums of Polynomials and Clique Roots ... In this paper, pursuing the same line of ideas in the proof of an old longstanding open conjecture of \\emph{Kadison-Singer} , we introduce a key lemma which we call it the interlacing lemma which indicates a necessary condition for having a real root for sums of polynomials with (at least) one real root.\nTitle: Sums of Polynomials and Clique Roots\nAuthors: Hossein Teimoori Faal\nDate: Fri Dec 17 20:07:25 2021\n\nIn this paper, pursuing the same line of ideas in the proof of an old longstanding open conjecture of \\emph{Kadison-Singer} , we introduce a key lemma which we call it the interlacing lemma which indicates a necessary condition for having a real root for sums of polynomials with (at least) one real root. Then, as an immediate application of this simple but potentially useful lemma we characterize several class of graphs which have only clique roots. Finally, we conclude our paper with several interesting open problems and conjectures for interested readers.--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nA flat graph whose clique polynomial has a nonreal root · trureturing knowledge (https://www.trureturing.org/knowledge/node/c026b4fdf2ce21eedcefaf11d0825b007cd17577f25c6a7636e2facc358ba1ae/)\nciteturn1search0 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 2 days ago; # A flat graph whose clique polynomial has a nonreal root\n\nFour complete four-vertex graphs joined in a ring give a twelve-vertex counterexample to Conjecture 1 of On Clique Roots of Flat Graphs.\n\nCombinatorics ClosedRELEASE 099187d7dec4\n\nOpen in Atlas Architecture evolution Papers & research bridges\n\nCombinatorics / CONCEPT\n\n# A flat graph whose clique polynomial has a nonreal root\n\nFour complete four-vertex graphs joined in a ring give a twelve-vertex counterexample to Conjecture 1 