l authority.\n\nRelease-bound static concept page.--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nA ring of four complete blocks refutes the flat-graph clique-root conjecture | trureturing (https://www.trureturing.org/research/teimoori-faal-2021-flat-graph-clique-roots-conjecture-1/)\nciteturn1search1 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 5 days ago; Teimoori Faal, On Clique Roots of Flat Graphs, arXiv:2112.09721v1, Conjecture 1, page 6, states: ... StatisticalMechanics.DimerVirialFourthDifferenceRefutation.Biconnected` and `3 ≤ Fintype.card V` | Connected before and after deletion of any vertex; more than two vertices | | $K_5$-free | `SimpleGraph.CliqueFree 5` | No five-vertex clique | | Has only clique roots | First conjunct of `claim` | Every complex zero has imaginary part zero | | $-1$ has multiplicity exactly two | Second conjunct of `claim` | `Polynomial.rootMultiplicity (-1) = 2` | | Implementation instances | `DecidableEq V`, `DecidableRel G.Adj` | Finite graph operations; no additional graph restriction | | Negative answer | `result : ¬ claim` | The first conjunct fails on one graph satisfying every hypothesis |\n\n# A ring of four complete blocks refutes the flat-graph clique-root conjecture\n\nLiterature status: not rechecked Repository record: refuted\n\nResolution source: D5/S3/Combinatorics/Graph/CliquePolynomial/TeimooriFaalFlatCliqueRoots.result10.48550/arXiv.2112.09721Source dossierRelease 36a49830636b\n\nProblem\n\n## The question\n\nH. Teimoori Faal, On Clique Roots of Flat Graphs, arXiv:2112.09721v1, Conjecture 1, page 6, states:\n\n> The class of 2-connected K₅-free flat graphs without isolated triangles has only clique roots. In particular, this class has always the clique root r = −1 of multiplicity 2.\n\nThe source note contains the definitions and locators. The preregistration is #19709. The quoted conjecture is Refuted by a twelve-vertex graph.\n\n### Statement echo\n\n| Source clause | Lean counterpart | Fidelity |